1
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:13,030
Three friends share prize money in the ratio 3 to 4 to 8, based on the hours each one worked.

2
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:16,040
The smallest share is 45 dollars.

3
00:00:16,090 --> 00:00:18,530
What was the total prize, in dollars?

4
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:22,090
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:24,810
The smallest share is 3 parts.

6
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:29,340
So 1 part is 45 divided by 3, which is 15 dollars.

7
00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:32,060
There are 15 parts altogether.

8
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:35,050
15 times 15 is 225 dollars.

9
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:41,760
Remember: to share 120 dollars in the ratio 4 to 5 to 6, add the parts: 15.

10
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:43,540
1 part is 8 dollars.

11
00:00:43,590 --> 00:00:47,400
The shares are 32, 40 and 48 dollars.

12
00:00:47,450 --> 00:00:54,050
Whatever you are given, a share, the total, or a difference, first find the value of one part.

13
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:54,740
Your turn.

14
00:00:54,790 --> 00:00:55,710
B has 4 parts.

15
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:57,790
What is B's share, in dollars?

16
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:01,060
Pause the video and try it.

17
00:01:01,110 --> 00:01:03,970
4 times 15 is 60 dollars.

18
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:08,490
Check: 45 plus 60 plus 120 is 225.

19
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:10,340
Ratios link to fractions.

20
00:01:10,390 --> 00:01:15,850
In 3 to 4 to 8, A gets 3 fifteenths, which is a fifth of the total.

21
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,220
Here is the method.

22
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:19,350
Step 1: add the parts.

23
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:25,700
Step 2: match what you know, a share, the total or a difference, to its number of parts.

24
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:28,910
Step 3: find one part, then multiply.

25
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:32,980
Step 4: check that the shares add up to the total.

26
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:36,560
In a club of 40, boys to girls is 3 to 5.

27
00:01:36,610 --> 00:01:39,080
That is 15 boys and 25 girls.

28
00:01:39,130 --> 00:01:40,560
4 more boys join.

29
00:01:40,610 --> 00:01:43,380
The new ratio is 19 to 25.

30
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:46,410
A map has a scale of 1 to 25,000.

31
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:53,860
6.4 centimetres on the map is 160,000 centimetres, which is 1.6 kilometres.

32
00:01:53,910 --> 00:01:54,600
Your turn.

33
00:01:54,650 --> 00:01:57,180
Two shares are in the ratio 5 to 2.

34
00:01:57,230 --> 00:01:59,700
The difference between them is 27.

35
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:01,030
What is the total?

36
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:04,050
Pause and work it out.

37
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:06,280
The difference is 3 parts.

38
00:02:06,330 --> 00:02:09,530
1 part is 27 divided by 3, which is 9.

39
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:12,220
The total is 7 parts: 63.

40
00:02:12,270 --> 00:02:13,630
Ratio 3 to 4 to 8.

41
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:16,310
A's share, 3 parts, is 45 dollars.

42
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,880
Nia finds the total.

43
00:02:17,930 --> 00:02:20,010
Which line is wrong?

44
00:02:20,060 --> 00:02:21,300
Line 1 is wrong.

45
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:24,850
45 dollars is 3 parts, not the total.

46
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:28,460
1 part is 45 divided by 3, which is 15.

47
00:02:28,510 --> 00:02:31,320
The total is 225 dollars.

48
00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:37,550
Business partners often share profits in the ratio of the money each one invested.

49
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:38,880
One last question.

50
00:02:38,930 --> 00:02:43,390
Concrete is cement, sand and gravel in the ratio 1 to 2 to 5.

51
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:47,080
What fraction is gravel: 5 eighths, or 5 sevenths?

52
00:02:47,130 --> 00:02:50,480
Pause the video and choose.

53
00:02:50,530 --> 00:02:52,730
There are 8 parts altogether.

54
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:55,690
Gravel is 5 of them: 5 eighths.

55
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:59,420
To remember: find the value of one part first.

56
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:03,600
You can start from a share, the total, or a difference.

57
00:03:03,650 --> 00:03:07,420
When a ratio changes, work with the real amounts.

58
00:03:07,470 --> 00:03:10,400
A ratio gives fractions of the total.

59
00:03:10,450 --> 00:03:15,790
Great work! Now practise lesson 11.1 on Camday.
